WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.990
Let's steal it and take it back to Dr. Eggman.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.860
What?

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.280
Can't you tell that we're mummies?

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.070
We're not severely injured people.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.410
Dr. Eggman wants to create the Eggman Empire.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:55.840
He planned to wipe out mankind by stimulating the world's bellybutton, causing all the volcanoes in the world to erupt.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:05.140
We went to the Gran Pacific Sea to stop him, but he was waiting for us with his new weapon, the Egg Giant Makan.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:10.060
With everyone's help, we freed Topaz who was being held hostage.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.690
However, Eggman disappeared into the mouth of the volcano.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.820
If we don't hurry up and go after him, there will be big trouble!

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.140
Episode 48

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.140
Sonic VS A Monster From Underground

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.510
We won't use our precious drill for something so pointless.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.390
We could've destroyed the Egg Giant Makan if you weren't taken hostage.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.100
Are you guys serious?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.390
Topaz!

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.640
Go, Tanaka.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.690
Thank you, sir.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.620
Topaz.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.710
I think the X-Cyclone can enter the crater.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.130
But it's dangerous.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.300
We know, but someone has to do it.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.930
Bat girl, what are you going to do?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.890
Going underground sounds like it'll be bad for my skin.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.510
But it would be perfect for an echidna.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.270
What did you say?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.140
Dr. Atsumi!

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.020
Look what we found.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.280
Is this harahirecon?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.650
Harahirecon?

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:45.120
It's a mysterious metal that the Murasia people used.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.040
It's beautiful!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:56.130
This treasure may have erupted out of the volcano from the sunken continent of Murasia.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.500
Or...

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.550
Does that mean there are more gems inside the volcano?

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.850
There's a tunnel over there.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.560
Just as I thought.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.520
"Just as I thought?" What's up with that?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.980
I know. He has no plan whatsoever.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.190
What are you secretly talking about?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.360
I'm going to tell Dr. Eggman!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.860
I have no clue what you're talking about.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.610
Me neither.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.160
You're so annoying!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.870
How's this?

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.590
X-Cyclone taking off!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.500
This section collapsed recently. Furthermore...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.290
In that case...

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:26.340
Stop, Sonic! All the dirt is unstable!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.640
Sorry.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.850
Although it's tiny, there's a tunnel here.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.850
I guess we have to take it.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.810
Sonic.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:40.310
Chris, will you help me?

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.660
Ouch!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.790
There are rocks everywhere, so be careful.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.920
Tell us that earlier!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.000
It's a type of luminous moss.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.300
Wow, you know a lot.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:10.470
Yeah. After all, I'm a treasure hunter who's traveled all around the world.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.220
Let's go.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.560
Yeah.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.480
Hey, listen to me when I'm talking!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.610
The moss is slippery. Be careful.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.950
Sorry.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.620
Will you please get off of me?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.930
Water!

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.390
It's fine. Once we cross, there's a path.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.020
No way. It'll ruin my makeup.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.600
Well, I should go help Chris.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.480
No excuses! C'mon!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.030
With all your makeup, you don't have to come if you don't want to!

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.280
I'm not wearing tons of makeup!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.500
I've had enough!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.300
I hear a waterfall.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.630
What? Is it the exit?

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.480
We can't go any further.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.560
Where are you going?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.190
Nice, Rouge!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.780
Sheesh...

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.500
What's up with this?

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.410
I don't know, but here's what I'm going to do.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.840
Hey!

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.220
What?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.850
Sonic!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.770
They're Murasia ruins!

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.570
What?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:38.830
The legend is true! After losing their land, they used harahirecon to create an artificial sun for their underground kingdom.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.080
They believed in dragons.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.330
However, ancient documents say they their dragon god destroyed them.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:54.260
They may have stimulated the world's bellybutton in order to calm down the dragon.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.220
A dragon doesn't sound scary.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.600
Isn't it just a big lizard?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.270
Even if it really exists, I'll knock it out with one punch!

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.480
You're so strong. I can depend on you.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.230
Stop teasing me!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.860
I'm just talking to myself.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:14.860
Or do you care how I think about you?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.320
Of course not!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.780
You guys, this isn't the time to fight.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.160
We have to find Eggman!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.910
I can tell this is going to be tough.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.880
Dr. Eggman, I'm hungry!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.220
I'm a bit hungry, too.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.550
Decoe and Bocoe, go find something to eat!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.560
Just us?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.810
Of course! Who else do I have?

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.640
Messenger Robo!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.480
I'm still a kid!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.570
I'm incapable of helping, you fool!

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.230
You heard him. We're expecting something nice.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.700
Go on.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.950
How annoying!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.000
It's set.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.580
Switch on.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.540
It's working properly.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:18.880
If we set another one here, we can analyze the magma flow to locate the world's bellybutton.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.390
There's nothing.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.010
I found something!

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.520
It's a slug!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.980
He'll be happy to eat it.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.770
He might complain that it's too soggy.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:30.520
You think?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.230
How about that?

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.070
That apple looks delicious!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.530
Let's take it back with us.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.140
It's you two!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.560
We should help them, Sonic.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.310
We don't need your help!

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:17.440
Since we're villains, we'll lose face if a hero helps us!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.740
Stop acting so tough!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.090
Chris!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.300
Chris...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.370
What are you doing?

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.750
He saved us from danger.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:15.960
What? And you call yourself minions of the evil genius, Dr. Eggman?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.210
Earthquake!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.670
Let's hang a mosquito net!

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:21.920
You do that for lightning!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:22.880
Oh yeah.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.640
That was scary.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.390
I wonder if Sonic is OK.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.440
They should be fine because it wasn't a big earthquake.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:44.200
The world's bellybutton is gradually releasing energy to maintain balance.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.240
What do you mean, Doctor?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:50.580
The underwater volcano is about to erupt.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:57.130
You'll also soon see the signs.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:01.760
When you do, you have to leave immediately, even if you haven't captured Eggman.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.670
Roger.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.220
What should we do, Sonic?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.720
There's no point waiting around here.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.640
I'm going to look for Chris.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.720
Hey, Sonic!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.140
We have such great teamwork.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.770
Where are you going?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.650
I'll search for him from the sky.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:23.440
You and Tails, set up your instruments and find the world's bellybutton.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.700
Eggman will definitely go there.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.620
Okay. I'm counting on you, bat- I mean, Rouge!

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.870
You're finally being true to yourself.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.250
You're like a moth to a flame.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:43.510
Since you saved these fools, you put Sonic in danger.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:47.010
Eggman!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.860
I'm lucky when I'm lucky.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:07.450
With that earthquake, I now know the location of the world's bellybutton!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.780
What are you doing? We're leaving immediately!

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.510
Wow!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.990
Bingo!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.990
Bocoe, the detonator!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:56.500
Right!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.420
Kid, this is the center of the world's bellybutton.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:06.880
If I blow up this location, all the volcanoes in the world will erupt in a chain reaction.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:14.970
After the world is destroyed, the genius scientist Dr. Eggman will create his new Eggman Empire!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.600
What will happen to Sonic?

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.810
For the sake of our friendship, I'll let you live.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.020
Here.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.440
You can't do this!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.110
What are you doing?

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.400
That was mean, Dr. Eggman!

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.530
He's just a kid!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.320
It's not my fault.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.210
This is a great view.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.750
I'm scared!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.070
You idiot!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.620
What's the fuss?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.190
Save me, Sonic!

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.230
Chris!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:49.610
Just in time.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.650
Rouge.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.090
You're heartless, Dr. Eggman!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.420
It's finally started.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:15.300
What's happening?

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.720
The underwater volcano has started to erupt.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.890
That's scary!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.310
We have to escape.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:33.820
The world's bellybutton will explode in eight minutes. We won't escape in time.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.280
You won't be able to do anything!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.710
Screw Kick!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.330
No way!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.430
This way, you monster!

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.900
Kid, wait!

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.310
Decoe! Bocoe!

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:15.240
If we don't repay our debt, it'll tarnish our reputations as villains.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.610
It's finally time to do it.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:20.450
Our legendary combo giant transformation!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.740
What? Can it be?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.550
Is that what's going to happen?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:44.390
Combine! Decoe Bocoe Cross!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:48.390
Huh?

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.520
I'm sorry. We lied.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:51.770
We can't do it.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.150
What?

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.110
Watch out!

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:03.200
Is this how we're going to die?

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.660
Decoe! Bocoe!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.750
Chris!

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.920
You guys!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:23.090
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:23.090
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:27.390
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:27.390
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.190
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.190
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.520
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.520
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.860
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.860
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.570
Pull yourself together!

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:41.950
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:40.900
Get ready!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:46.080
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:46.080
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.780
You're pretty good.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.950
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.950
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.250
Our attacks don't work.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.920
We'll manage somehow.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.670
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.670
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.000
Sonic, use this.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.040
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.040
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.210
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.670
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.590
It's lunchtime!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.670
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

